&nbsp;","Administrative Assistant for Entrepreneur Launching Multiple Businesses

Job Type: Part-Time (10–25 hours/week to start)
Compensation: $25–$35 per hour (DOE)
Location: Portland, OR (Hybrid or Remote for the right person)

About the Role

I’m an entrepreneur building several new ventures in real estate, AI technology, and lifestyle brands. I move quickly and value efficiency, organization, and clear communication. I’m looking for a smart, capable Administrative Assistant to help me turn big ideas into reality — someone who thrives on structure, keeps projects moving, and loves bringing order to creative chaos.

You’ll play a vital role in helping me launch and manage new businesses by handling administrative, organizational, and creative tasks that free me to focus on growth, partnerships, and strategy.
This role also includes supporting our social media presence — helping post updates, maintain content calendars, and share what we’re building with the world.

Key Responsibilities

Manage calendars, schedule meetings, and handle daily logistics
Organize email, files, and shared drives (Google Workspace)
Coordinate communications between partners, team members, and vendors
Track project milestones, tasks, and to-do lists
Conduct research (vendors, market trends, potential hires, tools, etc.)
Assist with light bookkeeping, expense tracking, and data entry
Support and maintain social media accounts (Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook, etc.)
Create, schedule, and post engaging content that reflects our brand and projects
Monitor engagement and help identify growth opportunities online

Ideal Candidate

You’re the kind of person who loves to get things done right the first time. You don’t wait to be told what to do — you look ahead, plan, and make it happen. You enjoy solving problems, organizing moving parts, and helping build something from the ground up.

You are:

Highly organized, reliable, and detail-oriented
Tech-savvy and quick to learn new systems and tools
Excellent at written and verbal communication
Proactive, resourceful, and creative
Comfortable balancing administrative and social media work
Excited about supporting entrepreneurial projects in growth mode

Preferred Skills

Experience supporting an executive, founder, or small business owner
Familiarity with Google Workspace, Notion, and task management tools
Comfort with QuickBooks, Excel, or light bookkeeping
Social media management experience (posting, scheduling, analytics)
Bonus: interest or background in real estate, startups, or AI

Schedule & Growth

Starts part-time at 10–25 hours per week, with a flexible schedule.
If it’s a great fit and the businesses continue to scale, there’s a strong possibility this position could grow into a full-time role.

To Apply

Please include:

A short introduction about yourself
Why this role and mission resonate with you
A few examples of how you’ve helped previous clients or employers stay organized, launch projects, or manage social media

