Administrative Support: Efficiently manage the CEO’s calendar, schedule meetings, and coordinate travel arrangements, ensuring all appointments and meetings are well-organized and effectively executed.
Communication Management: Handle all incoming and outgoing communications on behalf of the CEO, including emails, phone calls, and correspondence, ensuring timely and professional responses.
Document Preparation: Prepare and edit documents, presentations, reports, and other materials for the CEO, ensuring accuracy, clarity, and professionalism in all communications.
Project Coordination: Assist in the planning and execution of special projects and initiatives, tracking progress, managing timelines, and ensuring deliverables are met.
Meeting Coordination: Organize and coordinate internal and external meetings, including agenda preparation, meeting minutes, and follow-up actions, ensuring all necessary materials and information are available.
Confidentiality and Discretion: Handle sensitive information with the utmost confidentiality and discretion, maintaining a high level of professionalism at all times.
Office Management: Oversee the general organization and cleanliness of the executive office, ensuring necessary supplies and resources are available and maintained.
Public Relations Support: Assist in managing the CEO’s public relations, including drafting communications, coordinating media interactions, and maintaining a positive public image.

Qualifications:

Experience: Proven experience as an executive assistant or in a comparable supportive administrative capacity, with a demonstrated history of leadership and independent initiative. A background in the healthcare or physical therapy sectors is advantageous but not mandatory.
Skills: Exceptional organizational and time management skills, with a strong attention to detail and the ability to prioritize tasks effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills are essential.
Mindset: A servant-focused mindset with a strong desire to support and enhance the CEO’s effectiveness. The ability to work independently and proactively is crucial.
Attributes: High level of integrity, professionalism, and discretion. The ability to handle a fast-paced and demanding environment with grit and determination. Adaptability and the ability to manage changing priorities.
Technical Proficiency: Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and other relevant software tools.
Flexibility: The ability to work a flexible schedule to accommodate the needs of the CEO and the organization, ensuring a balance between professional and personal commitments.

Why Join Peak Performance Physical Therapy:

Impactful Work: Be part of a team dedicated to making a positive impact on the lives of our patients.
Professional Growth: Opportunities for personal and professional development within a dynamic and growing organization.
Supportive Environment: Work in a collaborative and supportive atmosphere where your contributions are valued."
