&nbsp;","Xcimer Energy leverages decades of research on Inertial Fusion Energy (IFE) combined with groundbreaking new laser architecture. Our mission is to deploy fusion power plants to meet global decarbonization goals as fast as possible. Xcimer has assembled a team of leaders in tough tech, fusion science, and manufacturing with a track record of rapid execution. Supported by leading investors, Xcimer is uniquely positioned to deliver limitless, clean, fusion power to combat climate change. Join us in powering a better world with inertial fusion!
As Executive Assistant, you are a key partner to the CEO, CTO, COO, and other senior leaders. You will manage complex calendars, anticipate needs, and create smooth workflows that allow leadership to focus on high-impact priorities. This role requires exceptional organizational skills, proactive problem-solving, and the ability to operate with discretion, speed, and polish.
Your success will come from thinking two steps ahead, building strong relationships, and ensuring that no detail falls through the cracks. We are looking for a people centric, customer service orientated Administrative Assistant to apply their organizational expertise, problem solving skills, and dedication to quality to positively impact the future of energy!

What Great Looks Lik in This Role:
Proactive: You identify issues before they become problems and offer solutions.
Detail Oriented: Your work is consistently accurate and complete.
Anticipatory: You understand priorities and stay two steps ahead.
Polished Communicator: Your written and verbal communication builds trust and credibility.
Calm Under Pressure: You keep things moving even in high-stakes situations.
Responsibilities
Executive Support & Prioritization:
Serve as the primary point of contact and gatekeeper for executive calendars.
Anticipate needs, resolve scheduling conflicts before they occur, and create space for priority work.
Keep leadership informed of upcoming commitments and ensure follow-up on action items.
Calendar Management & Meeting Management:
Maintain dynamic, high-volume calendars for multiple executives.
Plan, coordinate, and track all meetings, reviews, and appointments.
Prepare agendas, capture detailed notes, and ensure clear next steps are documented and communicated.
Travel & Logistics:
Arrange complex domestic and international travel, including itineraries and agendas.
Prepare all required documentation for travel related meetings.
Complete expense reports accurately and promptly.
Communication & Documentation:
Draft, proof, and edit professional correspondence, reports, and presentations.
Ensure all communications (internal and external) are clear, accurate, and polished.
Handle confidential information with the utmost discretion.
Event Planning & Coordination:
Plan and execute company events, offsites, board meetings and executive gatherings.
Manage meeting logistics, materials, and follow-up.
Own communication with external partners for event details, logistics, and agenda items.
Cross Functional Administrative Support:
When needed, assist with recruiting coordination, candidate interactions, onboarding activities, and cross-team project logistics.
Maintain office supply and equipment inventory in partnership with Administrative Assistants.
Ensure conference rooms and shared spaces are meeting ready.
Customer Service & Relationship Management:
Deliver a high level of service to all stakeholders (internal staff, external partners, candidates, and visitors).
Act as a trusted liaison between executives and other teams.
Qualifications
Experience: 5+ years of experience as an Executive Assistant preferably in a startup or fast-paced environment.
Proficient in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, and Power Point)
Excellent verbal and written communication skills, interpersonal skills, and high customer service capabilities with a keen attention to detail.
Proactive problem-solving skills and a willingness to take initiative.
Attention to detail and ability to produce quality products with a high level of accuracy.
Ability to multitask and prioritize tasks effectively in a dynamic and evolving environment.
Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion.
Ability to earn trust, influence others, and maintain positive and professional relationships.
Administrative skills, organizational skills, and problem-solving skills.
Comfortable in a fast-paced, dynamic, and ambiguous environment.
A positive attitude, with a customer service-oriented approach and a passion for working with people.
Must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee of granted asylum.
