Powered by one of the largest global newsrooms in sports media, The Athletic brings sports fans the most comprehensive stories about the teams, sports and athletes they love. The Athletic’s newsroom of 500+ full-time staff delivers in-depth coverage of hundreds of professional and college teams across more than 47 North American markets and all 20 football clubs in the English Premier League, as well as many Championship clubs.

About The Role

As Executive Assistant, you will provide operational administrative support to our Digital Leadership team, across product, engineering, data, and growth teams. Understanding basic company organization, working relationships and business partner roles and responsibilities is important as this position will work closely with other teams across The Athletic. This candidate is able to work successfully in a team environment, build effective working relationships inside and outside of the group, while keeping abreast of general business objectives, policies, standards, services and processes. As Executive Assistant, you will represent The Athletic brand, to both internal colleagues and external clients, and proactively approach tasks and requests effectively.



The ideal candidate is based in the greater New York City metropolitan area.

This is a hybrid role with a mix of an in office and remote working schedule.

This is a non-exempt, hourly position.
Responsibilities
Manage executive calendars, including coordinating meetings with participants, resolving conflicts, and generally managing the Digital Leadership team’s daily schedules.
Organize department meetings, including scheduling, reminders, agenda development, conference room and/or virtual room set-up, and technology support.
Attend key meetings, tracking and helping drive completion of key deliverables, and following up on outstanding items.
Serve as department administrator and maintain departmental organizational charts, vacation calendars, distribution lists, and more.
Prepare drafts of general correspondence, department communications, reports and presentations.
Lead logistics for All Hands meetings, departmental and team events, social activities, offsite meetings, etc as well as for external events which include, but are not limited to, client entertainment and advertising industry events.
Arrange travel, manage expense report processing and administer department credit card.
Answer questions from department staff, assisting in the resolution of general problems and coordinating with other teams (IT, HR, etc.) to support.
Field incoming requests, including to department email accounts, and direct them to appropriate teams, and handle highly confidential information with good judgment and discretion.
Build and manage relationships with various departments throughout the organization, as well as other administrative assistants.
Provide a wide range of operational support and assist with special projects as they arise.
