About My Easy Offer

Winston's Property Solutions is a fast-growing real estate investment company based in Plymouth, Michigan. We buy, renovate, and sell homes throughout the state, as well as manage a portfolio of rental and short-term airbnb properties. We’re a small, agile team driven by excellence, integrity, and results — and we’re looking for an organized, resourceful, and proactive Executive Assistant to support our business owner directly.

About the Role

This is a diverse, hands-on position designed for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys wearing many hats. You will work closely with the business owner to oversee the daily operations of active real estate deals, manage communications, coordinate projects, and help keep the business running smoothly.

The ideal candidate has a strong background in real estate transactions or operations, is highly organized, and enjoys taking ownership of projects from start to finish.

Key Responsibilities

Update and maintain the company’s active deal roster daily, managing all next steps for each deal
Track and update sales team KPIs daily
Manage and organize the business owner’s email inbox and communications
Oversee the transaction coordinator to ensure all deals reach the closing table (including occasional hands-on transaction coordination)
Assist with deal disposition and listing coordination
Manage and process company bills and payments
Oversee office operations, including cleanliness, organization, and supplies
Supervise and coordinate maintenance of 12 rental properties (including 7 Airbnbs in Plymouth)
Schedule and ensure weekly yard cleanings and hot tub maintenance
Conduct weekly property walk-throughs of renovation and fix-and-flip projects
Deliver materials to job sites using the company truck when needed
Coordinate contractor outreach and obtain bids for renovation projects
Support management of software systems and business tools
Perform miscellaneous tasks as needed to support the business owner and ensure smooth operations

Qualifications

Minimum 1 year of experience in real estate, property management, or a related field
Proven experience supporting executives or managing multiple operational functions
Strong understanding of real estate sales processes and transaction coordination
Excellent communication, organization, and problem-solving skills
Tech-savvy — comfortable managing spreadsheets, CRMs, and cloud-based systems
Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation
Ability to handle multiple priorities with attention to detail and professionalism

Benefits

$50,000 annual salary
10 days paid time off
Opportunity to work directly with the company owner in a dynamic, entrepreneurial environment
Growth potential within a rapidly expanding real estate business

How to Apply

If you’re motivated, detail-oriented, and eager to be part of a fast-paced real estate team, we’d love to hear from you. Please submit your resume and a brief cover letter explaining why you’re a great fit for this role.

