&nbsp;","We’re looking for an exceptionally organized, proactive, and detail-obsessed Assistant to the Founder/CEO to provide full-spectrum support across both personal and business life. This is a fast-paced, high-impact role that requires extreme ownership, discretion, and the ability to keep multiple moving pieces running seamlessly behind the scenes.

You’ll work directly with the Founder/CEO — managing her schedule, communication, travel, logistics, and operational priorities across multiple ventures and projects.

This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a dynamic startup environment, loves solving problems before they’re noticed, and takes pride in keeping everything (and everyone) organized and moving forward.

About the Companies

The Founder/CEO leads multiple ventures in the coaching and events space — including Community Building Collective, which helps community leaders around the world build profitable in-person event-based businesses, and Coffee & Chill Miami, a fast-growing social wellness event that brings together thousands of guests on a biweekly basis.

Together, these ventures blend entrepreneurship, creativity, and community — and you’ll play a vital role in keeping the operations behind them running smoothly.

Position Overview

As the Assistant to the Founder/CEO, you’ll act as her right hand — managing personal and professional logistics, overseeing operations across two companies, and ensuring projects, people, and priorities all move forward seamlessly.

You’ll handle everything from travel planning and scheduling to client follow-ups, event logistics, and partnership outreach. You’ll bring a proactive, Type-A, get-it-done mindset to every task — keeping the founder’s world organized and freeing her to focus on high-level strategy and creative leadership.

This is a hybrid position based in Miami, FL, with flexibility to work from home most days and in-person collaboration required as needed.

Key ResponsibilitiesFounder & Personal Support

Manage the founder’s calendar, inbox, and daily schedule with precision.
Coordinate personal tasks such as errands, appointments, and reservations in Miami.
Plan and manage travel — including flights, hotels, transportation, and itineraries.
Serve as a reliable point of contact for both personal and business matters, maintaining the highest level of discretion and professionalism.

Operations & Administration

Handle day-to-day administrative needs across two businesses — including data entry, documentation, and workflow coordination.
Manage client and partner follow-ups, ensuring timely communication and next steps.
Oversee partnership communication, outreach campaigns, and appointment scheduling.
Maintain up-to-date records, spreadsheets, and tracking systems for ongoing projects and deliverables.
Support project execution by managing to-do lists, timelines, and reminders — ensuring nothing falls through the cracks.

Systems & Process

Build and maintain organizational systems in tools like Notion, Google Drive, and Google Sheets.
Track and report on progress for ongoing initiatives, client engagement, and operations workflows.
Continuously identify opportunities to improve efficiency, automate repetitive tasks, and streamline communication.

Who You Are

Extremely Type A — detail-obsessed, methodical, and proud of it.
Proactive and hungry — you anticipate needs before they arise and take initiative without waiting for direction.
Hardworking and reliable — you thrive in a startup environment and aren’t afraid to get your hands dirty.
Excellent communicator — clear, professional, and polished in both written and verbal communication.
Emotionally intelligent — comfortable working closely with a founder and managing sensitive or confidential matters.
Tech-savvy — proficient with GSuite, Notion, Slack, and tools like Zapier or Go High Level.
Multi-tasker — able to shift seamlessly between personal and business priorities without missing a detail.

Bonus Skills

Experience with event coordination, partnership management, or social media operations.
Background in admin, operations, or project management within a startup or coaching business.
Comfortable with evolving priorities, fast pivots, and supporting a high-performance, entrepreneurial team.

