&nbsp;","Deck Hoss is looking for a driven Outdoor Living Sales Specialist to help homeowners design and build premium decks, pergolas, and outdoor living spaces throughout the Tulsa area.

This role combines design consultation with sales — you’ll meet with clients, guide them through materials and finishes, and present fixed-price proposals. To succeed, you must be confident in your ability to build trust, communicate value, and close deals.

While Deck Hoss provides marketing and some inbound leads, success in this position also depends on following up, building relationships, and creating new opportunities.

If you’re motivated, disciplined, and ready to grow with a brand that values integrity and craftsmanship, we’d like to meet you.

What You’ll Do

Develop and follow a clear sales plan to meet revenue goals for decks, pergolas, and outdoor living projects within the Tulsa metro area.
Meet with qualified homeowners to understand their vision, gather site details, and guide design and material decisions that fit their goals and budget.
Identify and pursue new business opportunities through networking, referrals, social media, and local outreach — not cold calling scripts, but genuine relationship building.
Prepare and present clear, fixed-price proposals that communicate value and craftsmanship.
Confidently negotiate and close sales, ensuring clients feel informed and comfortable every step of the way.
Track and manage leads, opportunities, and follow-ups using CRM tools to keep your pipeline organized.
Collaborate with marketing to strengthen local visibility and refine how we communicate our brand value.
Coordinate with estimating and production teams to ensure each signed project transitions smoothly to construction.
Provide excellent customer service before and after the sale — clear communication, honest expectations, and timely follow-up.
Stay aware of local market trends, material innovations, and competitor offerings to help Deck Hoss remain the trusted choice for premium outdoor living.

Skills & Qualifications

Proven experience in outside or in-home sales, preferably in construction, remodeling, or other design-build environments.
Strong relationship-building and account-management skills focused on long-term client satisfaction and repeat business.
Excellent negotiation and closing ability — confident asking for the sale while keeping integrity and professionalism.
Experience using CRM software (JobTread, Salesforce, or similar) to manage leads, track communication, and maintain accurate records.
Understanding of construction methods, materials, or outdoor living products is a plus — willingness to learn is essential.
Clear, confident communication skills, both verbal and written; able to present project concepts and pricing effectively to homeowners.
Self-motivated and organized, with the ability to manage follow-ups and sales activities without daily supervision.
Strategic thinker who can assess local market conditions and adjust approach to achieve sales goals.
Experience in lead generation, direct sales, or consultative selling within the home-improvement or construction industries.

Job Summary

This is a consultative sales position that combines design sense, construction knowledge, and relationship-building with the ability to confidently close sales. You’ll meet with leads, evaluate projects, develop fixed-price proposals, and walk clients through every detail with honesty and professionalism.

We’re a growing company built on craftsmanship, and integrity. To succeed in this role, you’ll need strong communication skills, disciplined follow-up habits, and a genuine commitment to helping clients make confident decisions.

If you’re self-motivated, organized, and ready to build a career where your results are valued and your reputation matters, Deck Hoss could be the right fit for you.

Job Type: Full-time

Pay: $40,000.00 - $60,000.00 per year

